@title The Island

You wake up in a small boat, drifting on a calm sea. In the distance you can see an island, with a thin column of smoke rising from the trees.

Do you [[row towards the island]] or [[stay where you are]]?

[[row towards the island]]:
You row until your arms ache, and the boat scrapes onto a sandy beach.

There are [footprints] in the sand, and an [old hut] at the top of the beach. A [[path]] leads into the trees.

[footprints]:
They're fresh, and they lead up towards the trees. Someone else is here.

[old hut]:
The door hangs off its hinges. Inside, there's a rusty lantern on the table.

[[path]]:
The path climbs through the trees, and ends at the mouth of a cave. The smoke is coming from inside.

[[stay where you are]]:
You drift for hours. The island grows smaller, and then it's gone.
